course: dictionary
lesson: 10023
title: Tendons: joining muscle to bone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tendon is a strong, tough band in the body that joins a muscle to a bone. Use the context to check: «The Achilles tendon joins the calf muscles to the heel bone.» The calf muscles and the heel bone are the clues, so a tendon must be the link between them.
explain: Muscles pull, and tendons pass that pull on to the bones. «When a muscle shortens, it pulls the tendon, which moves the bone.» That is how your leg can lift your foot when you walk or hop.
explain: Do not mix tendons up with ligaments. «Ligaments join bone to bone, while tendons join muscle to bone.» A quick check: if the word joins a muscle, it is a tendon.
fact: A tendon is a strong, tough band of tissue in the body.
fact: A tendon joins a muscle to a bone, so the muscle can move the bone.
fact: «The Achilles tendon» is the biggest tendon, at the back of the heel, and it is named after the Greek hero Achilles.
fact: «Red kangaroos» have springy tendons that make hopping use less energy.
fact: Ligaments join bone to bone, but tendons join muscle to bone.
exercise: «The Achilles tendon joins the calf muscles to the heel bone.» What does a tendon join? | *Muscle to bone | Bone to bone | Skin to skin | Water to blood
exercise: What is a tendon? | A small bone in the fingers | A soft, floppy bag that stores water | A type of blood vessel | *A strong, tough band that joins a muscle to a bone
exercise: «Ligaments join bone to bone, while tendons join muscle to bone.» Which pair does a tendon join? | Muscle and skin | Bone and bone | Two muscles | *Muscle and bone
test: «Red kangaroos» have springy tendons that make hopping cheap in energy. What do the tendons help the kangaroo do? | Stop them from hopping | *Hop using less energy | Grow taller every day | Keep their joeys warm
test: Which word joins bone to bone? | Tendon | Muscle | Joey | *Ligament
exam: Why does warming up in PE help your body? | It turns ligaments into muscles | It means you do not need a drink | *It helps protect tendons and muscles from injury | It makes your bones longer
